- The guest robots call under the name "insurance is coming due" or "medical reimbursement supplement is delivered" to direct the click on the insured link in the text message
- Direct deductions after clicking on the link, elimination of process complications

** This is not just a compliance issue - it reflects the possibility that companies may have resorted to aggressive, even transboundary, marketing under growth pressures**

# Two readings #

** A rigorous reading**: The ABC's complaints model (AI exterior call + text message quote + automatic deduction) is highly systematized, not a violation by individual employees, but a problem with the design of the business model**. The Jang Sodo Tai acquired in 2023 was precisely the one that operated the AI call-out user – which means that "disturbing marketing" may not be by-products, but rather a warm built capacity.

** Moderately read**: The generally high rate of complaints in the insurance brokering sector is not unique to the warmness. 248 complaints are low for a company that deals with tens of millions of class cases a year. The regulatory authorities have not yet imposed substantive penalties on Aeys, suggesting that the problem may not be as serious as they might be.

** Key judgements**: In any case,** a company about to be listed, whose subsidiaries are named by the Xinhua News Agency for reporting complaints,** will be followed up at the Hong Kong border hearing. If not handled properly, this may affect the listing process.

